{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And his spirit was troubled.</b> From the nif'al conjugation, like נפעמתי ולא אדבר (Psalms 77:5). Some say it is all from the root הולם פעם (Isaiah 41:7), and the meaning is that the spirit is likened to a body that is struck:" "<b>My magicians.</b> A quadriliteral word, and it may be Aramaic or Egyptian, and they are the scholars of nativities:" "<b>And all its wise men.</b> In the constellations and the interpretation of dreams:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:38.011176786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}